{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2f36d62d4ed3c19aed46cee8d8374062e6431f183eff730991124ce7a7601a91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The MCP Observer acts as a transparent proxy on port 9999 between Claude Code and any HTTP-based MCP server, with the destination URL configured at runtime via a dashboard page."},{"claim_ids":["clm_579dec6d2009efef92f3f6c1c09f2945cb56f07b4d608ffca444720fcf2b26cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: CLAUDE.md imposes a writing style rule for documentation, forbidding em dashes and dashes as sentence separators in README.md and other docs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_791dfcc0cf71e770528e6616582349dae29b4438246c69c6b41b500426f7eafb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Captured data is held in memory only: a circular buffer capped at 1000 requests for API traffic, plus in-memory stores for hook events and MCP requests (max 500), with no persistence."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2f36d62d4ed3c19aed46cee8d8374062e6431f183eff730991124ce7a7601a91","clm_579dec6d2009efef92f3f6c1c09f2945cb56f07b4d608ffca444720fcf2b26cb","clm_791dfcc0cf71e770528e6616582349dae29b4438246c69c6b41b500426f7eafb"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_45c46896e5c942bb95d4cd12b20b6b1e","id":"pg_2375c98520bf525f9460da36a289bd13","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/tndata-codingagentexplorer-claude-md-e70b2cc5213e-da36a289bd13.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9930a9445ce75614bbe568d29e0e9012"],"title":"tndata/CodingAgentExplorer/CLAUDE.md @ e70b2cc5213e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_45c46896e5c942bb95d4cd12b20b6b1e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08f07587ff2efaa6205faf4a6eb56e79017965b9a2dd3eb6164a92327780b769"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claude Code is pointed at the proxy by setting the ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL environment variable to http://localhost:8888; helper scripts enable and disable it per terminal session only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_112fc3d9ce852c49e1cc2794e4a6a31e0acf5162e45d91509c84e9cd1da42a9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: build and run with 'dotnet build' then 'dotnet run --project CodingAgentExplorer'; publish via publish.bat (Windows) or bash publish.sh (macOS/Linux) into a gitignored Published/ directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_15f3990fb8a930384735f5d4d8363949fc738965e66188bcdcd3a1139c862b60"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HookAgent is a companion CLI used as a Claude Code hook command: it reads a JSON payload from stdin, collects Claude environment variables, POSTs to the dashboard's /api/hook-event endpoint, and relays exitCode/stdout/stderr back."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2f36d62d4ed3c19aed46cee8d8374062e6431f183eff730991124ce7a7601a91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The MCP Observer acts as a transparent proxy on port 9999 between Claude Code and any HTTP-based MCP server, with the destination URL configured at runtime via a dashboard page."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5808aef265d2b075d3a69bf5e5b24db221ad5aa012b83866a7126bebdaed059c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The dashboard exposes three views: HTTP Inspector (table of proxied requests with headers, bodies, SSE events, timing), Conversation View (chat-style timeline), and MCP Observer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5a4ce8633bf5bfc9a61c36f2a8c0f2c83863e985fe33fd316642463746a6db43"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HookAgent exits silently with code 0 when the dashboard is not running, so it never blocks Claude Code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_791dfcc0cf71e770528e6616582349dae29b4438246c69c6b41b500426f7eafb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Captured data is held in memory only: a circular buffer capped at 1000 requests for API traffic, plus in-memory stores for hook events and MCP requests (max 500), with no persistence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_84c037f3ba48863afadefb13f7bf72a3210b2c482ccac708b0dc52ce06328fd5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool currently supports Claude Code with the Anthropic API only; support for additional coding agents may be added in the future."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae14e7c49873ebf6842aeae4f02799a9b5d72bb8cde7216292918866b2f1d38e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project was built as a teaching tool for AI-agent workshops, helping developers understand what happens under the hood when AI coding agents work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c74b8dd5f97bbf4ea2462ba86411efe02d2fabf596d7639f2bb9c77acdc2faf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"API keys in x-api-key and Authorization headers are automatically redacted from stored request data, and the proxy listens only on localhost."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf1f1562b7de53c4cb5ff4fd1726fb60b48f2149d8f9948c543f8f7ebabd49d0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool runs four localhost endpoints: reverse proxy on 8888, MCP proxy on 9999, and dashboard on 5000 (HTTP) and 5001 (HTTPS, auto-launching a browser on Windows)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e657275eb07badb388230cec2064cbfadacf50c477151585e467255fc5ce2fe6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture uses ASP.NET Core with YARP reverse proxy, SignalR for real-time dashboard updates, a vanilla HTML/JS/CSS frontend with no build step, and a single NuGet dependency (Yarp.ReverseProxy)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e7b85008fafe429202bf14cddc449be828a58f162b7b499b869efe51d6bf4b21"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project requires the .NET 10 SDK (or later) to build, and published outputs require the .NET 10 runtime on the target machine."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08f07587ff2efaa6205faf4a6eb56e79017965b9a2dd3eb6164a92327780b769","clm_112fc3d9ce852c49e1cc2794e4a6a31e0acf5162e45d91509c84e9cd1da42a9f","clm_15f3990fb8a930384735f5d4d8